    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18585" root="سأل" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُؤَلَةٌ</span></b> , (S, K,) also pronounced <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُوَلَةٌ</span>, (TA,) A
man (S) <i>who asks,</i> or <i>begs, much;</i> (S, K;) as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَأّ=لٌ</span></b> , and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَؤُولٌ</span></b> : (TA:) such is improperly
termed ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَائِلٌ</span></b> . (Durrat el-Ghowwás, in De
Sacy's Anthol. Gramm. Ar., p. 47 of the Ar.
text.)

